    rdfs:label "urn:silmaril:entity#instances.papers.11_base_commutative_diagram.chapters.10_alternatives_dual_computational.sections.01_alternative_formalizations.concrete_anchor_12_hdirectanimalinference#h_direct_animal_inference" .
silm:instances_papers_11_base_commutative_diagram_chapters_10_alternatives_dual_computational_sections_01_alternative_formalizations_concrete_anchor_12_hdirectanimalinference#h_direct_animal_inference silm:hasLongDescription "The h_direct_animal_inference is the direct h:Mittens->Animal leg; admissible only when h=g.f.c (path equation). In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'h_direct_animal_inference', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
